From cf49d5881a331d91647aa60471b2cb95b6f888b4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CosmosEx Buildroot <4372835+planeturban@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 00:16:37 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ce_main_app: encrypted backups with passwords and keys

The backup download leaves passwords and keys out by default (ce-backup).
POST /api/v1/system/backup/download with "secrets" and a "password"
includes them and encrypts the whole file: AES-256-GCM, key from the
password with PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA256 (200000 rounds), header authenticated,
tag at the end. The restore upload decrypts it first with the password
from X-Backup-Password (URL-encoded): a wrong password or a damaged file is
refused before anything changes.
---
